# Stack Decisions (do not re-litigate)
- Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript. Tailwind CSS. shadcn/ui — minimal set only (button, card, badge, separator).
- Motion: GSAP 3 + ScrollTrigger + `@gsap/react` + Lenis. Custom split-text helper — no Club GSAP plugin. Do not add `motion`, Framer Motion, or a fourth animation library.
- Palette: forest `#0E2A26`, cream `#F3EEE4`, mustard `#E4B52A`, sage `#9BB3A0`. Display font: Fraunces. Body: Geist. Tags: JetBrains Mono.
- Content lives in local TypeScript files under `content/` — no CMS, no database, no auth. Real content comes from `portfolio-spec.md`, not invented.
- Contact: mailto/social links by default; no backend unless explicitly requested.
- Deploy target: Vercel.

# Folder Structure
```
src/
  app/
    page.tsx              → the one-page homepage, composes section components
    projects/page.tsx     → projects archive grid
    projects/[slug]/page.tsx  → case study route (areej, exam-io)
    cv/page.tsx           → branded in-site PDF viewer
  components/
    sections/               → Hero, About, TechStack, Projects, ProjectsIndex, Cv, CvPage, Contact
    shared/                 → Navbar, Footer, and non-motion primitives
    motion/                 → SmoothScroll, SplitHeadline, StickyStack, ScrollPath, ParallaxLayer, StaggerIn, IconStrip
    ui/                     → shadcn primitives, untouched/generated
  content/
    profile.ts                → bio, tagline, contact links
    skills.ts                  → tech stack groups
    projects.ts                 → project + case-study data (Areej, Exam.io)
    cv.ts                      → CV viewer chrome (route, labels, PDF + preview image)
  lib/                        → utils, gsap register, split-text helper
public/
  cv/                          → Amar-Ibrahim-CV.pdf + preview.jpg
```
Route files in `app/` stay thin — they compose section components, no content or business logic inline.

# Naming Conventions
- Folders: kebab-case. Component files: PascalCase.tsx. Hooks: camelCase.ts, prefixed `use`.
- Types: PascalCase, no `I` prefix.

# Clean Code
- No prop drilling past 2 levels.
- One component = one responsibility.
- No `any` — use `unknown` + narrowing, or fix the type.
- No hardcoded copy inside components — all real content comes from `content/*.ts`.
